        "abstract": "Over the past six years, four Environmental Monitoring Systems have been installed at the Atomic Energy Authority's site at Dounreay in areas handling radioactive materials. The systems purpose is the collection and data processing of signals from a large number of radiation monitors and ancillary detectors and the display of the data to plant operators and Health Physicists. Their essential function is twofold: as a surveillance system with alarm level monitoring of all monitors, and as a short term data logger, recording activity levels on all monitors.<<ETX xmlns:mml=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\">&gt;</ETX>",
